# Documentation rules

## Style

- Complete sentences; clear headings; tables for reference data
- Link between docs with relative paths (`[Guide](ARCHITECTURE.md)`)
- Code blocks with language tags (`bash`, `powershell`, `sql`)
- Keep port examples aligned with `.env.example` (5174, 3002, 8010)

## When to update

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New API route | `docs/API_REFERENCE.md`, `README.md` API section |
| New env var | `.env.example`, `docs/EXTERNAL_SERVICES_SETUP.md`, `backend/config.py` |
| Agent Hub behaviour | `docs/AGENT_HUB.md` |
| Trip pack / PDF / email | `docs/TRIP_PACK.md` |
| Security change | `SECURITY.md` |

## Accurate product facts

- LLM default: Groq (not Gemini)
- Postgres 15 in Docker
- Trip pack requires all three planners
- Feedback survey email: after all three planners (separate from trip plan PDF button)
- Package names: Love Nest Getaway, Together Time Package, custom packages when weak match

## Do not

- Document unimplemented features
- Include real API keys or passwords in examples
